Silicone oil distribution transformers are electrical transformers that use silicone-based insulating liquid for dielectric insulation and heat transfer. These transformers are designed for applications where thermal stability, electrical reliability, and fire-performance considerations influence equipment selection.
The market is developing as hospitals, commercial buildings, data centers, transportation facilities, and industrial installations seek dependable electricity distribution equipment suitable for demanding operating environments.
Silicone insulating fluids provide an alternative to conventional mineral oil in appropriately engineered transformer designs. Their thermal characteristics can support applications where fire-related installation requirements are particularly important.
